rementing and decrementing the correct numerical result of the right-hand side, handling non-numeric results by offering \"None\" and \"0\". The choices are then sorted numerically to prevent the correct answer always appearing in the same position. Finally, the function returns a question, choices, the correct index, the correct value, and an explanation.\n\nVerifying that `step.predictQuestion` is being attached to each step, I will examine `enrichTraceWithExplanations(traceResult)` to confirm this and check if `step.teachingSubsteps` exist. Inside these substeps, ensure `s.predictQuestion = step.predictQuestion`.\n\n\nThe UI elements confirm the presence of an animation toggle, a prediction question toggle, and a speed control. The prediction card, hidden by default, indicates an interactive learning phase involving outcome prediction questions. The `btnToggleQuiz` element's title and text suggest the quiz feature is initially disabled.\n\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css","EndLine":250,"StartLine":190,"toolAction":"Viewing btn-subtle in styles.css","toolSummary":"View btn-subtle in styles.css"}}]}
